# The `this` arm of the pass-over refusal over a map that keeps a member beside the scalar passed over,
# inside a block over the member: `Config` holds `Mode` beside `Inner`, which lacks both keys and is kept
# in the map's place, and `Config` itself lacks both keys, so the filter is refused; the console shows the
# whole text, the definition of `X` and the remedy first; no sub-map holds either key, so the remedy is
# the one-object spelling.
rule r {
    Resources.WebServer.Properties.Configuration.Config {
        this[ ServerSideEncryptionConfiguration !exists LoggingConfiguration !exists ] empty
    }
}
